.SH NAME
niac-list-captures - List packet captures


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac list captures [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List packet captures from the content library. Captures are the
PCAP/PCAPNG/CAP files used by replay, packet inspection, and offline analysis
workflows.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for captures


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--root\fP=""
	Library root (default: NIAC_LIBRARY_ROOT or ~/.niac/library)

.PP
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # List installed captures
  niac list captures
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac-list(1)\fP


